OL,3,ATrump posthumously pardons US baseball
OL,4,Alegend Pete Rose
OL,5,
OL,6,FUS President Donald Trump has
OL,7,Fposthumously pardoned baseball legend
OL,8,FPete Rose.
OL,10,F"I have just given a Complete and Total
OL,11,FPardon to the Late, Great Pete Rose, a
OL,12,Ftrue Baseball SUPERSTAR & LEGEND,"
OL,13,FTrump wrote on Truth Social on
OL,14,FThursday.
OL,16,FRose, who died in 2024 at the age of
OL,17,F83, pleaded guilty in 1990 to two
OL,18,Fcounts of filing false tax returns. He
OL,19,Fwas also given a lifetime ban from
OL,20,FMajor League Baseball (MLB) after an
OL,21,Finvestigation revealed he bet on games.
OL,23,APub: 19-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,320,300,200,140,0,100
